}_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2z-2{e}^{-z}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2z-2{e}^{-z}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[2z+{z}^{2}+2{e}^{-z}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(2+1+2{e}^{-1})-2{e}^{0}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}1+2{e}^{-1}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}1+2{e}^{-1}\\,dy & =(1+2{e}^{-1})[y]_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =(1+2{e}^{-1})(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =2{e}^{-1}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345836 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345837 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345838 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345839 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345840 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345837 13194139535361 true] [17592186345835 1110 #uuid "52075f2e-7b6e-5241-b6d3-25133ec49afd" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345836 1034 "8-3e" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345836 1111 #uuid "29fd257e-187d-560a-8c07-c8cb5d56ce03" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345837 1034 "2{e}^{-1}+1" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345837 1111 #uuid "b9842096-2ee3-5bb7-9d74-ac9cd5d88db5" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345838 1034 "3-{e}^{2}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345838 1111 #uuid "dd842b71-aba2-5250-a4bd-b50a300b283b" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345839 1034 "3{e}^{-1}-2" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345839 1111 #uuid "525ec21c-bf14-5005-bcd9-ab9cb6c117d1" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345840 1034 "4{e}^{2}-1" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345840 1111 #uuid "933dc5e5-8d51-5602-b9f5-cdf0d13b16fe" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345841 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345842 13194139535361 true] [17592186345841 1089 "q-161581" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535361 true] [17592186345841 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le y+z+2},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the $z$-axis and the line $z=2-y$ in the first quadrant." 13194139535361 true] [17592186345841 1113 #uuid "42f45f71-27d5-5a4a-be80-b08c3b688e33" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345841 1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z+2}y\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z+2}y\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+z+2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y(y+z+2)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/b473cc75dbbd6fa36ba43f6bbdec4a0133164e6fd8bc5f76ff86cec74714a256.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[({y}^{2}+2y)z+\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}+2y)(2-y)+\\frac{1}{2}y(2-y)^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4y-{y}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}y(4-4y+{y}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}+6y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =-2-\\frac{16}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345843 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345844 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345845 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345846 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345847 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345843 13194139535361 true] [17592186345842 1110 #uuid "c4a19db3-df16-55a0-ac05-56ac3de3c554" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345843 1034 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345843 1111 #uuid "ff8365eb-0de9-505e-a99e-5929f21f44cf" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345844 1034 "3" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345844 1111 #uuid "3dedf070-9163-5bfd-8414-8c71f4114c84" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345845 1034 "\\frac{23}{6}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345845 1111 #uuid "8334554d-e6c0-5719-a407-6eb5431ecb41" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345846 1034 "\\frac{19}{2}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345846 1111 #uuid "6fa5a7d7-33f6-5f78-b0ab-11f41d5afd8f" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345847 1034 "4" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345847 1111 #uuid "58c7ff58-467d-5623-8910-3ba05fda5413" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345849 13194139535361 true] [17592186345848 1089 "q-161583" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345848 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535361 true] [17592186345848 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le yz},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z={y}^{2}$ in the first quadrant." 13194139535361 true] [17592186345848 1113 #uuid "38ba2e71-6d19-5a55-bf3c-392d867b639c" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345848 1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(yz)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/acb173db9d28ed8b38e63c7bc365c20e5755aeb1af3f6340e7b9229a4b49101d.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z={y}^{2}}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}({y}^{6}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{8}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{9}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{9}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345850 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345851 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345852 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345853 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345854 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345851 13194139535361 true] [17592186345849 1110 #uuid "be55cf0f-6150-574d-9a8d-38e9c2d7d650" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345850 1034 "\\frac{11}{12}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345850 1111 #uuid "84f03db3-b90c-5c71-a84b-d3de3a197ccd" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345851 1034 "\\frac{1}{27}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345851 1111 #uuid "4e843926-8cd5-5599-9b8b-9ad831c075b5" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345852 1034 "\\frac{2}{9}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345852 1111 #uuid "b9cdf12f-b650-56de-b7f7-5d76c8840ef6" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345853 1034 "\\frac{5}{18}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345853 1111 #uuid "1b97ccb1-aa79-5691-9343-9914ab8a8e51" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345854 1034 "\\frac{1}{16}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345854 1111 #uuid "9d71eca6-3e03-5d88-a34c-f94eeaa9a608" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345855 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345856 13194139535361 true] [17592186345855 1089 "q-161585" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345855 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535361 true] [17592186345855 1100 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z=-{y}^{2}$ in the fourth quadrant." 13194139535361 true] [17592186345855 1113 #uuid "411a3ab9-0aa0-5668-8896-afd110dee3fc" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345855 1145 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/38ea49a6fae41574107b2ba68a578586a306cf43d419d4de5699dcfa009137c2.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[({y}^{2}+1)z+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-{y}^{2}}^{z=0}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1)((0-(-{y}^{2}))+\\frac{1}{3}(0-{(-{y}^{2})}^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1){y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{21}{y}^{7}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{105}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345857 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345858 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345859 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345860 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345861 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345860 13194139535361 true] [17592186345856 1110 #uuid "be53cb49-8a48-5762-aeaa-2ef555c03209" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345857 1034 "\\frac{72}{121}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345857 1111 #uuid "31002da7-5aa8-5131-bed9-bfe5d9350bae" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345858 1034 "\\frac{34}{81}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345858 1111 #uuid "3e3c6399-6607-5c87-93e7-f06e701d6c3a" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345859 1034 "\\frac{79}{100}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345859 1111 #uuid "587e8c04-ddd1-5ee5-8403-ec1c90247522" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345860 1034 "\\frac{61}{105}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345860 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345860 1111 #uuid "2c023ca5-9eba-556b-996c-b06fca980833" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345861 1034 "\\frac{67}{92}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345861 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345861 1111 #uuid "4dc6af97-65f4-578e-b92a-db5b854954b5" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345863 13194139535361 true] [17592186345862 1089 "q-161589" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535361 true] [17592186345862 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/d5690bff5819d72cc9d49016c119dc79f62f4d766c142a43a89df196ce9f2335.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345862 1113 #uuid "d80c8b49-f108-517b-a5d1-42a714175231" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345862 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/2427e053c0e2d808b32db5d7fedf81365e7e50f0b3f2dc61598ad1795394686e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+2y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2+2y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{y}^{2}z+2{y}^{3}z-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345864 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345865 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345866 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345867 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345868 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345867 13194139535361 true] [17592186345863 1110 #uuid "ebd964e0-ee68-5278-b55d-92ee733d2366" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345864 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345864 1111 #uuid "566221f6-05f9-5a62-ad5d-a14b8f6663c2" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345865 1034 "2" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345865 1111 #uuid "4af2d5c0-c18a-5b00-bca0-f4d7f21685c5" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345866 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345866 1111 #uuid "fc8d7283-92d8-5679-a77a-192d04ac0f4a" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345867 1034 "1" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345867 1111 #uuid "9b823093-1d5d-5b2c-81ca-cd77e7019fba" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345868 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345868 1111 #uuid "23da081d-2cec-5f18-9eae-59476b85ed61" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345869 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345870 13194139535361 true] [17592186345869 1089 "q-161594" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345869 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535361 true] [17592186345869 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/f1f3493cd1ff0bee115bf7c311504a2b8a9bbd38dd35adae96c9f7abcae40ae1.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V=$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345869 1113 #uuid "9f7a494d-dd58-51ac-963c-d9b00a8df0cd" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345869 1145 "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/6cc327f63d7141c43852e868812a7cff1ec9ae0acfed636ff896ceb204b6fbf0.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\n(y-1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=1\\,⟺\\,z=\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a0fb19d32c2545e5c2a61cbb54536e7c28b1a54dbce51c7752c3687035d6c3d6.png)\n\nHence, $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}[{x}^{2}]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345871 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345872 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345873 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345874 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345875 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345873 13194139535361 true] [17592186345870 1110 #uuid "2c8e251d-48b1-5631-af6f-1b4cd3f362c4" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345871 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345871 1111 #uuid "a2f1afdc-c843-5ee1-bb6c-447b29d9f822" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345872 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345872 1111 #uuid "15b050f1-9e57-5b74-80e1-ff2e2422124e" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345873 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345873 1111 #uuid "15c5bfac-7a70-5074-b840-4cbd1d14a9d5" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345874 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345874 1111 #uuid "137455a8-e5cd-540f-9859-24f40273b3fc" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345875 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-(y-1)^{2}}}3z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345875 1111 #uuid "d79a42bd-4ffe-5589-9366-db84c051c4e6" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345877 13194139535361 true] [17592186345876 1089 "q-161783" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535361 true] [17592186345876 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/3fe3ec24f8f8006f22bde8ba2dc39fd3cd3f73668b06f8ea4a74e4ed5206a193.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345876 1113 #uuid "61ab6bf1-137b-57a1-bf89-390949bf96b6" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345876 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/2a20f2651c24e48871028b44fe61da4600d632481877ef32ccdfd3241262a53b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1ba7c02f254313a73a813e4e43c44c25523ce77dd47e594a1db3b412a6bd5c3d.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=5-y-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}(5-y-\\frac{z}{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{z}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy & =[2y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =6-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345878 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345879 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345880 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345881 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345882 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345880 13194139535361 true] [17592186345877 1110 #uuid "cd620578-dd05-5846-bced-85b22a8b4888" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345878 1034 "12" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345878 1111 #uuid "81f5c9aa-ae0a-53ad-af70-47d8421072c6" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345879 1034 "3" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345879 1111 #uuid "f9f7c3d4-0e9c-5b1a-b1d5-dd75f724d77a" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345880 1034 "6" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345880 1111 #uuid "242096ed-d41a-5d6d-98e1-028871bfa249" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345881 1034 "1" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345881 1111 #uuid "83ff5443-55a6-5aac-82c7-b81c2cfd2eca" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345882 1034 "4" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345882 1111 #uuid "d26d4c23-36ab-5376-82dd-b1fed6968883" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345883 1017 #edb/ref 17592186345884 13194139535361 true] [17592186345883 1089 "q-161784" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345883 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535361 true] [17592186345883 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/ca49b92d602d04a73dc7ab9936d601654bd293ce3fb7950372ac86155875aca3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345883 1113 #uuid "d31e4325-59b1-526f-a289-64b327737018" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345883 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/0008ba406cfe8a5b61d683a6854260897cb441752a5333add281ab1279e31b0b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/bbe6b6b897e5d53421080ae8e8b9dc49f2ea1b7e135f8426ee3f11af01cc2401.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}(2-\\frac{y}{3}+z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy & =[y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345885 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345886 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345887 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345888 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345889 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1041 "selection" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345886 13194139535361 true] [17592186345884 1110 #uuid "c8270bc6-063c-537c-bfa3-2431ffe6f033" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345885 1034 "9" 13194139535361 true] [17592186345885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535361 true] [17592186345885 1111 #uuid "b00137a0-9917-53ee-8915-833087c8b564" 13194139535361 true] [17592